  {
    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "page_id": "topic-14-5",
    "page_path": "/explore/media/advertising-and-marketing/",
    "name": "Advertising & Marketing",
    "level": 2,
    "parent_path": "/explore/media/",
    "entity_type": "category",
    "address": null,
    "phone": null,
    "email": null,
    "website": null,
    "logo": null,
    "contact_source_ids": [],
    "description": "Advertising and marketing in Iran connect businesses with audiences through commercial messages, content, and distribution channels. Domestic advertising services operate within a wider environment shaped by platform restrictions, internet controls, and rules governing electronic commercial communication.",
    "tags": ["Advertising", "Marketing", "Commercial communication", "Digital media", "Consumer protection"],
    "status": null,
    "editorial_status": "needs_research",
    "as_of_date": "2026-10-26",
    "created_at": "2026-10-28T08:44:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-28T08:44:03Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Advertising and Marketing in Iran: Channels and Constraints",
      "description": "Understand Iran’s advertising channels, domestic platforms, commercial communication rules, and the limits of available market evidence."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "understanding-the-field",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A field spanning messages, media, and measurement",
        "content": "Advertising purchases or arranges exposure for a commercial message. Marketing is the broader work of understanding an audience and connecting an offer with its needs. For this guide, the subject is divided into digital advertising, search engine marketing, social media marketing, content marketing, outdoor advertising, and advertising effectiveness. These branches overlap: a campaign may use an explanatory article, a paid placement, and a landing page while measuring their contribution together.\n\nIran’s domestic providers illustrate some of that overlap. Yektanet’s service catalogue includes website and application advertising, messaging, search-related services, and agency work. Tapsell lists web and in-application formats alongside placements associated with particular consumer services. Their catalogues establish what the companies advertise as available services; they do not independently establish market leadership or customer results. [s1][s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "channels-and-objectives",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Channels serve different purposes",
        "content": "The distinction between a format and an objective is useful when reading Iranian advertising material. A banner is a presentation format; attracting recognition or generating an enquiry is an objective. Tapsell’s catalogue separates banners, video, native advertising, retargeting, and application-install services. That variety shows why the term digital advertising cannot be reduced to paid search alone. [s2]\n\nContent marketing concerns useful or explanatory material intended to build a relationship with an audience. Search engine marketing concerns discovery through search, while social media marketing concerns communication within social platforms. Outdoor advertising places messages in physical settings. These distinctions organize the guide; they are not estimates of each branch’s share of Iranian expenditure. No verified national spending breakdown is presented here.",
        "source_ids": ["s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "access-and-platforms",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Platform access shapes distribution",
        "content": "International advertising infrastructure cannot be assumed to operate in Iran on the same terms as elsewhere. Google’s inspected policy lists Iran among the places where Google Ads is unavailable to advertisers and restricts location targeting. A domestic agency’s offer of Google-related services does not, by itself, establish that a particular advertiser or campaign is eligible under Google’s rules. [s3]\n\nIranian internet controls introduce a separate constraint. Freedom House’s 2024 assessment documents filtering, disruptions, and policies favouring domestic services during its reporting period. This is historical evidence of the operating environment, not a live list of blocked platforms in October 2026. The distinction matters because advertising depends on whether an audience can actually reach the publication, application, or destination carrying a message. [s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s3", "s4"]
      },
      {
        "id": "commercial-rules",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Commercial messages and consumer information",
        "content": "The Electronic Commerce Act text available through WIPO Lex includes provisions against misleading marketing, requires clear information about advertised goods and services, and calls for the beneficiary of an advertisement to be identifiable. These provisions show that electronic advertising is also a consumer information issue. They should not be read as a complete statement of all advertising rules or of present enforcement. [s5]\n\nFor readers, the useful question is whether a message makes its commercial purpose and responsible business understandable. A polished presentation does not establish the accuracy of the underlying offer. Equally, a legal provision establishes a stated obligation, rather than demonstrating that every advertiser complies with it. [s5]",
        "source_ids": ["s5"]
      },
      {
        "id": "interpreting-performance",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Reading performance claims carefully",
        "content": "Provider websites combine service descriptions with promotional statements about reach and effectiveness. Those statements require different treatment. A listed format can establish that a provider markets that service; a claim of superior results requires evidence about the campaign, comparison, and measurement method. The inspected Yektanet and Tapsell pages do not supply an independent national benchmark for advertising effectiveness. [s1][s2]\n\nA useful account of this field therefore keeps channel availability, commercial rules, and demonstrated outcomes separate. The sources establish a varied domestic service landscape and significant access constraints. A fuller picture still requires dated evidence on broadcast and outdoor advertising, regional markets, and comparable expenditure. Until those gaps are resolved, this page is an introduction to the field rather than a complete market assessment. [s1][s2][s3][s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2", "s3", "s4"]
      }
    ],
